1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Listen to a talk in a history class.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,140
If you think about it

3
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:09,100
thanks to e-mail and computers we hardly write letters on paper anymore.

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,340
Most people don't even pay bills through the mail anymore

5
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:16,100
or mail informs to schools or to the government.

6
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,000
It seems almost everything can be done online now.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,950
Keep in mind though that e-mail is a very recent development,

8
00:00:23,950 --> 00:00:27,400
but postal services systems for delivering physical paper letters

9
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,978
and documents and other items,

10
00:00:28,978 --> 00:00:32,210
well, they have been around for a long time.

11
00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:35,880
For example, we know that in ancient times

12
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:39,160
documents were transported by riders on horseback.

13
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:41,820
They usually used a relay system

14
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:44,226
which means that one mail carrier would travel a certain distance

15
00:00:44,226 --> 00:00:48,420
with the mail and then pass it on to someone else

16
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:51,080
whose job was to take it the next part of the way.

17
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:53,600
In ancient China, for example

18
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:59,030
the government set up a large network of stations, where fresh horses were kept.

19
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:05,110
So mail carriers could deliver official documents to far away parts of the kingdom more quickly.

20
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:09,120
Now during the Roman Empire, almost two thousand years ago

21
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:12,056
Roman rulers established their own system of roads

22
00:01:12,056 --> 00:01:16,300
and stations for mail delivery across the Empire's vast lands.

23
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:20,635
Interestingly, even after the Roman Empire ended, its postal system remained intact;

24
00:01:20,635 --> 00:01:26,053
in other words, even though there was no official Roman Empire to govern the territories,

25
00:01:26,053 --> 00:01:31,110
the people living in the area found the postal system created by the Empire

26
00:01:31,110 --> 00:01:34,000
so useful that they continued to use it.

27
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,588
Then about five hundred years ago, during the Renaissance in Europe,

28
00:01:38,588 --> 00:01:41,900
different countries began to travel farther and farther

29
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:44,010
when they started trading goods.

30
00:01:44,010 --> 00:01:49,120
This led to a need for commercial documents to be delivered quickly and safely.

31
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:54,160
That's when private business got involved and started their own postal systems.

32
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:57,382
So now it wasn't only government that were delivering mail,

33
00:01:57,382 --> 00:02:01,190
and that's pretty much what it is like in the world today.

34
00:02:01,190 --> 00:02:04,450
Most governments operate their own postal services,

35
00:02:04,450 --> 00:02:10,039
but there are also many private companies that deliver letters and documents.

36
00:02:10,039 --> 00:02:15,130
Of course, with today's technology, there may soon be no need for any of them.
